---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="Terms" description="Terms of use for the IPJunction website.">
  <PageHead kicker="Legal" title="Terms of use" lede="Last updated October 6, 2026. Draft pending legal review." />
  <section class="section container prose legal">
    <p>By using this website you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.</p>

    <h2>Information only</h2>
    <p>
      Content on this site, including Insights articles, is general information. It is not professional advice for your
      situation, and no client relationship is formed by reading it or contacting us. Engagements are governed by a
      separate written agreement.
    </p>

    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The site's text, design and logo belong to {SITE.legalName} unless stated otherwise. Client and third-party names
      are used to describe past work and remain the property of their owners. You may quote short passages with
      attribution and a link.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Some features use third-party services such as Cal.com and Web3Forms, which have their own terms. We are not
      responsible for third-party sites linked from this one.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      We work to keep the site accurate, but it is provided as is, without warranties. To the extent the law allows, we
      are not liable for losses arising from its use.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We may update these terms. The date at the top shows the latest version.</p>

    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of New Jersey, USA.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
